When the app is confused, we get bugs because confused code doesn't know which rule to apply. Confused code takes the path of least resistance.
Confused code trusts the nearest value it can find. Every one of those resolutions is an unintended behavior the developer never thought about. 
And look, I'm not telling you to hunt IDORs specifically. I love broken access controls, but the message here is not "go hunt IDORs."
The message is that understanding what you are dealing with without getting confused yourself is what makes these bugs show themselves.
